hey everyone I'm Dan Belcher and I'm a  product manager on the Google cloud  platform team at Google we spend a lot  of time thinking about how we can make  operations easier whether you're running  at Google scale or you're a new startup  looking to launch your first application  last month we announced the beta release  of Google Cloud monitoring which is our  effort to make monitoring easier in the  cloud in this session we'll give you a  quick overview of cloud monitoring and  its capabilities Google Cloud monitoring  gives you insight to keep your  application fast and available for  end-users the cloud monitoring console  gives you an at a glance view into the  overall health of your application  including your app engine modules groups  of resources such as compute engine VMs  or cloud sequel instances endpoint  checks which measure uptime of your  internet facing resources active  incidents or alerts KPIs or recent  changes and events within your  application with no configuration cloud  monitoring provides you with rich  dashboards and charts that you can use  to identify bottlenecks or issues with  key metrics you can also configure  alerts so that you're notified when  issues occur the system supports a  number of different communication  methods including email pager Duty SMS  HipChat campfire and more cloud  monitoring also includes rich support  for popular open source packages such as  Cassandra my sequel engine X and others  for instance you can use the monitoring  plug-in for engine X to gain access to a  variety of engine X metrics finally you  can tailor the monitoring experience to  your own needs with a few clicks you can  create custom dashboards that include  metrics from different components of  your system  and you can access advanced charting  tools to investigate issues cloud  monitoring is available to all Google  cloud platform users in beta you can  access cloud monitoring from any of your  projects by clicking on the monitoring  link in the left-hand menu and then  clicking dashboards and alerts cloud  monitoring is an important part of how  we're making operations easy at Google  you can learn more about cloud  monitoring today by signing up for the  beta or accessing the monitoring  documentation from cloud.google.com  slash monitoring
 

